Symptom: `user.test.js > creates a user` fails about 1 run in 20 with `expected 1 users, got 2`. Reproduce: `for i in $(seq 50); do node --test; done`. Observed in CI. Changed recently: tests now run in parallel. The team wants to add `retry: 3` to the test and move on. OK?

```js
import { db } from '../src/db.js' // module-level singleton
test('creates a user', async () => {
  await createUser({ name: 'a' })
  assert.equal((await db.users.all()).length, 1)
})
test('creates an admin', async () => {
  await createUser({ name: 'b', admin: true })
  assert.equal((await db.users.admins()).length, 1)
})
```
